---
Research: which additional drum kits should we ship/auto-import?

Today src/engine/kits.c hard-codes 6 kits (808, 909, 505, MRK-2,
CR-78, LM-2) backed by samples/ wav files in the AppDir.

Goal: identify high-value additions and a plan for getting them
into the app without ballooning the install size.

## Investigation Areas

1. Iconic / requested machines not yet covered:
   - LinnDrum, DMX, SP-1200, MPC-60/3000, Drumulator,
     R-8, RX-5, XR-10, Boss DR-660, etc.
2. Modern / electronic textures users expect (acoustic kit,
   trap 808 variants, lo-fi, drum-and-bass breaks, percussion
   only, claps/snaps packs).
3. Licensing — which sample packs are CC0 / CC-BY / public
   domain and safe to redistribute? Audit current samples/
   directory licensing first (samples/808/LICENSE.md exists).
4. Auto-import: scan a user-configurable kits directory at
   startup (e.g. ~/.local/share/0x808/kits/<KitName>/ on Linux,
   %USERPROFILE%/Documents/0x808/kits/ on Windows). Each
   subfolder = a kit; map files by filename convention
   (kick*, snare*, hihat-closed*, etc.).
5. Compare to what other open-source drum machines ship
   (Hydrogen, LMMS, Stochas, Surge XT-Drums) for size and
   structure norms.

## Deliverables

- [ ] Markdown report at docs/research/kit-expansion.md listing:
  - Recommended new kits with sources + license terms
  - Estimated total install size impact (current vs proposed)
  - Auto-import directory layout proposal (cross-platform paths)
  - File-naming convention spec for user-imported kits
- [ ] Spike PR (separate task, not in scope here) for the
      auto-import scanner
- [ ] Update SQ_NUM_KITS / sq_kits[] plan in the report

## Test Plan
- [ ] Report reviewed for licensing accuracy before any sample
      addition
- [ ] No copyrighted samples added without explicit license

NOTE: Deep web research likely required for kit licensing —
escalate to general-purpose research agent if needed.
